WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.797 --> 00:00:14.659
Perda sat near a big tree, thinking.

2
00:00:15.379 --> 00:00:19.640
A few hours had passed since she, Fala, Darb, and Gliss had joined the rebels.

3
00:00:20.381 --> 00:00:22.261
But to Perda it felt like a few years.

4
00:00:23.021 --> 00:00:24.982
Nothing was happening except lots of talking.

5
00:00:25.702 --> 00:00:27.062
And Zann still hadn't shown up.

6
00:00:27.823 --> 00:00:30.683
What if he hadn't been able to escape from the palace after that fall?

7
00:00:31.324 --> 00:00:32.824
Gliss and Darb wandered over to her.

8
00:00:33.824 --> 00:00:35.765
"What are the adults talking about now?"

9
00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:36.725
Perda asked.

10
00:00:37.406 --> 00:00:39.266
Darb sat down and gave Zing a pat.

11
00:00:39.286 --> 00:00:41.507
"Same stuff," he replied.

12
00:00:41.527 --> 00:00:46.089
"Half of them want to try Fala's plan to ride our dragons to the fortress and free Morb's

13
00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:51.111
prisoners. The others think we should just stay here and spy on Morb until we know what he's

14
00:00:51.171 --> 00:00:52.111
planning to do next.

15
00:00:52.792 --> 00:00:56.733
They say that until we know Morb's plans, there's no point in doing anything."

16
00:00:57.814 --> 00:00:59.174
Perda looked at the group of adults.

17
00:00:59.915 --> 00:01:03.076
Fala was still huddled with her friend Shem and some of the rebel leaders.

18
00:01:03.808 --> 00:01:07.271
"Seems like the only thing these rebels do is talk," Perda said.

19
00:01:08.051 --> 00:01:11.253
Gliss glanced up at the patch of sky that was visible through the trees.

20
00:01:11.273 --> 00:01:14.296
"It'll be getting dark soon," she said.

21
00:01:14.316 --> 00:01:17.718
"We should check the meeting spot again to see if Zann's there yet."

22
00:01:18.659 --> 00:01:23.482
A whisper of excitement ran through the camp as a spy fly buzzed into the clearing and headed

23
00:01:23.522 --> 00:01:25.463
for Vig, the leader of the rebel group.

24
00:01:26.504 --> 00:01:28.866
He was a tall, lean man with droopy eyes.

25
00:01:28.886 --> 00:01:31.588
"What's the spy fly showing you, Vig?"

26
00:01:31.932 --> 00:01:34.674
someone asked after the fly had burrowed into Vig's ear.

27
00:01:35.655 --> 00:01:40.238
Perda held her breath; the rebel leader closed his eyes to focus on the spy fly's message.

28
00:01:40.258 --> 00:01:43.900
"It found Morb," Vig said after a moment.

29
00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:49.204
"I'm not sure this place is the palace though—I also see a dungeon.

30
00:01:50.125 --> 00:01:52.386
I've never heard of a dungeon at the palace."

31
00:01:53.527 --> 00:01:55.308
"There is one," said a woman.

32
00:01:55.689 --> 00:01:57.430
"It dates back to the Old Times.

33
00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:02.325
But our king and queen have never imprisoned people—they just use it for storage."

34
00:02:03.525 --> 00:02:04.346
"Not anymore."

35
00:02:04.926 --> 00:02:06.246
Vig closed his eyes again.

36
00:02:06.266 --> 00:02:09.168
"It's full of Red prisoners now."

37
00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:10.628
Perda gasped.

38
00:02:10.888 --> 00:02:13.710
"Did Morb recapture the people we rescued from the zoo?"

39
00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.331
"I don't think so," said Vig.

40
00:02:16.771 --> 00:02:17.871
"I see Boz.

41
00:02:18.712 --> 00:02:20.313
The king and queen are there too."

42
00:02:21.493 --> 00:02:23.654
There were murmurs of confusion from all around.

43
00:02:23.674 --> 00:02:27.175
"Are you sure you're seeing the palace and not Morb's fortress?"

44
00:02:27.556 --> 00:02:28.156
Fala asked.

45
00:02:28.936 --> 00:02:31.678
Vig nodded grimly as the spy fly flew out of his ear.

46
00:02:31.698 --> 00:02:33.179
"I'm sure.

47
00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:38.223
It looks like Morb somehow transported all of his prisoners to First City."

48
00:02:39.103 --> 00:02:39.804
Vig gulped.

49
00:02:39.824 --> 00:02:43.727
"I can't imagine how much magic that must have taken."

50
00:02:44.948 --> 00:02:45.668
Shem spoke up.

51
00:02:45.688 --> 00:02:49.431
"We need to go back to the palace and rescue those prisoners."

52
00:02:50.311 --> 00:02:51.892
"How do you propose to do that?"

53
00:02:52.313 --> 00:02:52.873
asked a woman.

54
00:02:52.893 --> 00:02:56.596
"We must attack Morb at once," said someone else.

55
00:02:57.468 --> 00:03:01.030
"Morb is much too powerful," muttered an older man.

56
00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:04.231
The adults continued to argue about what to do next.

57
00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.592
Perda had heard enough.

58
00:03:06.832 --> 00:03:10.054
"Let's go check for Zann," Perda whispered to Gliss and Darb.

59
00:03:10.754 --> 00:03:14.295
The three of them slipped away from the clearing, with Zing flying just overhead.

60
00:03:14.315 --> 00:03:19.217
"I wonder if Zann knows that Boz is in the palace now," Darb said as they walked.

61
00:03:19.237 --> 00:03:21.859
"Do you think my parents are there too?"

62
00:03:22.259 --> 00:03:23.239
Gliss sounded anxious.

63
00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.672
"Probably," Perda said.

64
00:03:25.692 --> 00:03:28.794
"But why would Morb bring all those Reds to First City?

65
00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:32.095
Isn't he worried that they'll be easier to rescue there?"

66
00:03:32.115 --> 00:03:33.796
"I doubt it.

67
00:03:34.196 --> 00:03:38.178
Morb thinks he'll be able to control everyone's magic soon," Darb pointed out.

68
00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:43.480
By then they had reached the clearing, where the two cloud gliders grazed in the tall grass.

69
00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:47.362
Light from the setting sun shimmered gently across their scales.

70
00:03:47.382 --> 00:03:51.023
"Nobody's here except the dragons," Gliss said.

71
00:03:51.963 --> 00:03:52.904
Perda's heart sank.

72
00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:54.941
"I hope Zann is okay."

73
00:03:54.961 --> 00:03:57.883
"I'm sure he's fine," said Gliss.

74
00:03:57.903 --> 00:04:02.205
"Yeah," said Darb, "Zann knows how to take care of himself.

75
00:04:02.945 --> 00:04:04.346
He'll find a way out of the palace."

76
00:04:05.006 --> 00:04:06.227
Perda wasn't reassured.

77
00:04:06.247 --> 00:04:11.770
"Maybe we can convince the rebels to send out a search party tomorrow morning to look for Zann."

78
00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:16.373
Just then a twig snapped as a figure walked into the clearing.

79
00:04:16.393 --> 00:04:20.535
"You don't need to send out a search party," said a familiar voice.

80
00:04:20.555 --> 00:04:22.156
"I'm right here!"

81
00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:29.247
After checking on the prisoners in the dungeon, Morb returned to the upstairs room to await Wyssa.

82
00:04:29.987 --> 00:04:31.088
"Where is she?"

83
00:04:31.488 --> 00:04:31.928
he muttered.

84
00:04:31.948 --> 00:04:35.210
"It's bad enough she protected Boz's grandson.

85
00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:37.191
Now she keeps me waiting!"

86
00:04:38.192 --> 00:04:44.015
Morb needed Wyssa for one last, very important errand—to fetch a batch of blue leeches.

87
00:04:44.935 --> 00:04:49.638
Then his machine would be fully operational, and he would no longer have to rely on the old

88
00:04:49.718 --> 00:04:53.820
woman. It was past nightfall, and Wyssa still hadn't arrived.

89
00:04:54.588 --> 00:04:55.809
Morb grew furious.

90
00:04:55.829 --> 00:04:57.930
"This is ridiculous!

91
00:04:58.771 --> 00:05:00.092
Where is she?"

92
00:05:00.752 --> 00:05:02.834
He waved a hand and called up the Directory.

93
00:05:02.854 --> 00:05:06.997
"Wyssa!" he commanded when the translucent screen appeared before him.

94
00:05:07.977 --> 00:05:09.638
Wyssa's entry slowly formed.

95
00:05:10.419 --> 00:05:12.740
It was short, and many of the sections were blank.

96
00:05:13.681 --> 00:05:17.944
There was a notation at the top: "No longer a resident of Magica."

97
00:05:18.704 --> 00:05:21.006
"There must be some mistake," Morb grumbled.

98
00:05:21.706 --> 00:05:23.708
He glared at the Directory and cleared his throat.

99
00:05:24.384 --> 00:05:27.327
"Provide details," he ordered loudly.

100
00:05:27.347 --> 00:05:30.369
"Individual not currently in Magica.

101
00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:34.292
No possessions of individual currently in Magica.

102
00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:38.176
Individual is presumed to be permanently off-world."

103
00:05:39.557 --> 00:05:42.359
"No!" Morb gnashed his teeth.

104
00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.662
In a fit of rage, he blasted a hole in the wall.

105
00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:50.085
"Without those leeches, my machine is useless!"

106
00:05:51.046 --> 00:05:53.008
Morb stepped over to look out the big hole.

107
00:05:53.796 --> 00:05:55.979
Slib was hurrying past in the courtyard below.

108
00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:00.084
Morb's fury faded and was replaced by determination.

109
00:06:00.825 --> 00:06:03.409
Wyssa was gone, but maybe Morb didn't need her.

110
00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:08.575
After all, he was the king, and he had absolute authority over his subjects.
